# At the repo root, not in backend/, because the images build with the repo as their context: the
# web image needs `frontend/` and `deploy/nginx/`, and Docker resolves one ignore file per context.
#
# Without this the build context carries `backend/.venv` and `frontend/node_modules` — hundreds of
# megabytes uploaded to the daemon on every build, to be discarded by the first COPY.

# Virtualenvs and package trees — reinstalled inside the image from the lockfiles
**/.venv
**/venv
**/node_modules

# Build output. `frontend/dist` especially: the image builds its own, and copying a host build in
# would let a stale local bundle win over the one CI just produced.
frontend/dist
frontend/coverage
backend/staticfiles
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info

# Tooling caches
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.coverage
**/coverage.xml
**/htmlcov

# Runtime state that belongs to a machine, not an image
backend/media
**/*.sqlite3
celerybeat-schedule*
celerybeat.pid

# Secrets. Belt and braces — `.env` is gitignored too, but a build context is assembled from the
# working tree rather than from git, so an untracked .env would otherwise be baked into a layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# History and local notes
.git
.github
docs
Documentation
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode
